30) Equivalence of AR(1) and MA(infinity)

To better understand the relationship between MA models and AR models, you will demonstrate that an AR(1) model is equivalent to an MA(infinity) model with the appropriate parameters.
You will simulate an MA model with parameters 0.8, 0.8^2, 0.8^3, ... for a large number (30) lags and show that it has the same Autocorrelation Function as an AR(1) model with phi = 0.8.
Note, to raise a number x to the power of an exponent n, use the format x**n.

# import the modules for simulating data and plotting the ACF
from statsmodels.tsa.arima_process import ArmaProcess
from statsmodels.graphics.tsaplots import plot_acf
# Build a list MA parameters
ma = [.8**i for i in range(30)]
# Simulate the MA(30) model
ar = np.array([1])
AR_object = ArmaProcess(ar, ma)
simulated_data = AR_object.generate_sample(nsample=5000)
# Plot the ACF
plot_acf(simulated_data, lags=30)
plt.show()
=> Notice that the ACF looks the same as an AR(1) with parameter 0.8.

